---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../site.config';
import { measurementId } from '../analytics/consent';
const analyticsEnabled = !!measurementId(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy & cookies | UV GO"
  description="How UV GO uses local storage, weather services and optional Google Analytics cookies, and how to manage your choice."
  ogImage="/og/home.png"
>
  <article class="glass article-prose mx-auto max-w-3xl rounded-[22px] px-5 py-6 sm:px-8 sm:py-8">
    <h1>Privacy &amp; cookies</h1>
    <p>Last updated: 6 November 2026.</p>
    <h2>Who runs this site</h2>
    <p>
      UV GO is maintained by {siteConfig.author.name}. For privacy enquiries, contact the maintainer
      through <a href={siteConfig.author.url}>their GitHub profile</a>. Please do not post personal
      information in public issues.
    </p>
    <h2>Your weather preferences</h2>
    <p>
      Your selected place and planning preferences are stored in your browser’s localStorage. You
      can remove them by clearing this site’s data in your browser. Coordinates and city searches
      are sent to Open-Meteo to retrieve weather and location results. See
      <a href="https://open-meteo.com/en/terms">Open-Meteo’s privacy information</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>Optional Google Analytics</h2>
    {analyticsEnabled ? (
      <p>
        Analytics is available on this build. It runs only if you choose “Accept analytics”.
        Rejecting it does not limit access to the site. Before acceptance, we do not load Google’s
        analytics script or send analytics requests to Google.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>Google Analytics is disabled on this build. No analytics script is loaded.</p>
    )}
    <p>
      If enabled and accepted, Google Analytics 4 measures visits and site usage for audience
      statistics. Google Ireland Limited and Google LLC process usage data such as page paths, visit
      times, browser and device information, and cookie identifiers. Your IP address is transmitted
      when connecting to Google. We do not intentionally send your selected weather location, search
      terms, URL query parameters or fragments to Analytics. Advertising storage, advertising
      personalisation and Google signals are disabled in our tag.
    </p>
    <p>
      Analytics processing is based on your consent (Article 6(1)(a) GDPR). GA uses first-party
      cookies named <code>_ga</code> and <code>_ga_*</code> to distinguish visits. Their lifetime is
      limited to 180 days by this site’s configuration, without renewal on each visit. The analytics
      consent choice (acceptance or rejection, timestamp and version) is stored in localStorage
      under <code>uvgo:analytics-consent:v1</code> for 180 days. This preference is necessary to
      remember your choice and is not sent to Google by our consent manager.
    </p>
    <h2>Change or withdraw your choice</h2>
    <p>
      When analytics is available, use “Cookie settings” in the footer of any page to change your
      choice. Select “Reject analytics” to withdraw consent. This stops future collection, deletes
      accessible GA cookies for this site and reloads the page to remove the active tag. Withdrawal
      does not affect the lawfulness of processing before withdrawal and does not delete data
      already received by Google. Clearing site storage also resets your choice.
    </p>
    <h2>Google’s processing and your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Google may process data outside the European Economic Area, including in the United States.
      Its contractual safeguards and applicable transfer arrangements are described in
      <a href="https://business.safety.google/adsprocessorterms/">Google’s data processing terms</a>
      . Read <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s Privacy Policy</a> and
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">
        how Google uses data from partner sites
      </a>
      .
    </p>
    <p>
      Under applicable data protection law, you may request access, correction, erasure or
      restriction of your personal data, and portability where applicable. Contact the maintainer
      using the link above. You may also lodge a complaint with your local data protection
      authority.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
